rence/mathacademy/question-capture/13964951/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-35831" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=\\frac{7}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964951/state.json" "file_sha256" "794a5b783a2e6ed149688ecb4d1509c96dad9ea40a695092ba12b68371dbf4c9" "basis" 655 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964951/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-35831" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the horizontal asymptote of the function $f(x)=\\frac{14{x}^{3}}{6{x}^{3}+1}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070044/state.json" "file_sha256" "fcf78247d9a402fb67e5db2c4ea4f7384ca3af6e70cc708b70481b8ad348a81b"} {"question" "q-35831" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The horizontal asymptote is $y={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }f(x).$ To find the horizontal asymptote, we apply the usual procedure of dividing the numerator and denominator by the highest power of $x$ in the denominator, which is ${x}^{3}.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{14{x}^{3}}{6{x}^{3}+1} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{14{x}^{3}}{{x}^{3}})}{(\\frac{6{x}^{3}}{{x}^{3}}+\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{14}{(6+\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}})} \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{6+0} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the horizontal asymptote of $f(x)$ is $y=\\frac{7}{3}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070044/state.json" "file_sha256" "fcf78247d9a402fb67e5db2c4ea4f7384ca3af6e70cc708b70481b8ad348a81b"} {"question" "q-35831" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070044/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b0e21228d6346ad940cb7128271d38a4af8b3b4e91929c8c6677236e432cb17f"} {"question" "q-35831" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070044/state.json" "file_sha256" "fcf78247d9a402fb67e5db2c4ea4f7384ca3af6e70cc708b70481b8ad348a81b"} {"question" "q-35831" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=0"] ["math" "y=2"] ["math" "y=\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "y=\\frac{7}{3}"] ["text" "No horizontal asymptote"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070044/state.json" "file_sha256" "fcf78247d9a402fb67e5db2c4ea4f7384ca3af6e70cc708b70481b8ad348a81b"} {"question" "q-35831" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=\\frac{7}{3}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070044/state.json" "file_sha256" "fcf78247d9a402fb67e5db2c4ea4f7384ca3af6e70cc708b70481b8ad348a81b"} {"question" "q-68068" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the horizontal asymptote of $y=f(x)$ where $f(x)=\\frac{4{x}^{3}+6}{5x}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070044/state.json" "file_sha256" "fcf78247d9a402fb67e5db2c4ea4f7384ca3af6e70cc708b70481b8ad348a81b"} {"question" "q-68068" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The horizontal asymptote is $y={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }f(x).$ To find the horizontal asymptote, we apply the usual procedure of dividing the numerator and denominator by the highest power of $x$ in the denominator, which is $x.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{4{x}^{3}+6}{5x} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{4{x}^{3}}{x}+\\frac{6}{x})}{(\\frac{5x}{x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(4{x}^{2}+\\frac{6}{x})}{5} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(4{x}^{2}+0)}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{5}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }{x}^{2} \\\\  & =\\infty .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe limit does not come out to a finite number. Therefore, there is no horizontal asymptote." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070044/state.json" "file_sha256" "fcf78247d9a402fb67e5db2c4ea4f7384ca3af6e70cc708b70481b8ad348a81b"} {"question" "q-68068" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070044/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b0e21228d6346ad940cb7128271d38a4af8b3b4e91929c8c6677236e432cb17f"} {"question" "q-68068" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070044/state.json" "file_sha256" "fcf78247d9a402fb67e5db2c4ea4f7384ca3af6e70cc708b70481b8ad348a81b"} {"question" "q-68068" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-\\frac{4}{5}"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "\\frac{4}{5}"] ["text" "No horizontal asymptote"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070044/state.json" "file_sha256" "fcf78247d9a402fb67e5db2c4ea4f7384ca3af6e70cc708b70481b8ad348a81b"} {"question" "q-68068" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "No horizontal asymptote"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070044/state.json" "file_sha256" "fcf78247d9a402fb67e5db2c4ea4f7384ca3af6e70cc708b70481b8ad348a81b"} {"question" "q-101312" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{{x}^{3}-x}{{x}^{2}-3}=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070044/state.json" "file_sha256" "fcf78247d9a402fb67e5db2c4ea4f7384ca3af6e70cc708b70481b8ad348a81b"} {"question" "q-101312" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we divide both the numerator and the denominator by the highest power of $x$ in the denominator, which is ${x}^{2}.$ Then, by noting that the reciprocals shrink to $0$ in the limit, we can then evaluate the resulting expression.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{{x}^{3}-x}{{x}^{2}-3} & ={lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{{x}^{2}}-\\frac{x}{{x}^{2}})}{(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}}-\\frac{3}{{x}^{2}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{(x-\\frac{1}{x})}{(1-\\frac{3}{{x}^{2}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{x-0}{1-0} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }x \\\\  & =-\\infty .\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070044/state.json" "file_sha256" "fcf78247d9a402fb67e5db2c4ea4f7384ca3af6e70cc708b70481b8ad348a81b"} {"question" "q-101312" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070044/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b0e21228d6346ad940cb7128271d38a4af8b3b4e91929c8c6677236e432cb17f"} {"question" "q-101312" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070044/state.json" "file_sha256" "fcf78247d9a402fb67e5db2c4ea4f7384ca3af6e70cc708b70481b8ad348a81b"} {"question" "q-101312" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\infty "] ["math" "1"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{3}"] ["math" "\\infty "] ["math" "\\text{DNE}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070044/state.json" "file_sha256" "fcf78247d9a402fb67e5db2c4ea4f7384ca3af6e70cc708b70481b8ad348a81b"} {"question" "q-101312" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\infty "] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070044/state.json" "file_sha256" "fcf78247d9a402fb67e5db2c4ea4f7384ca3af6e70cc708b70481b8ad348a81b"} {"question" "q-302235" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\,\\,\\frac{8{x}^{6}+5}{2{x}^{5}-7x}=$\n\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070044/state.json" "file_sha256" "fcf78247d9a402fb67e5db2c4ea4f7384ca3af6e70cc708b70481b8ad348a81b"} {"question" "q-302235" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we divide both the numerator and the denominator by the highest power of $x$ in the denominator, which is ${x}^{5}.$ Then, by noting that the reciprocals shrink to $0$ in the limit, we can then evaluate the resulting expression.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\,\\,\\frac{8{x}^{6}+5}{2{x}^{5}-7x} & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\,\\,\\frac{(\\frac{8{x}^{6}}{{x}^{5}}+\\frac{5}{{x}^{5}})}{(\\frac{2{x}^{5}}{{x}^{5}}-\\frac{7x}{{x}^{5}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\,\\,\\frac{(8x+\\frac{5}{{x}^{5}})}{(2-\\frac{7}{{x}^{4}})} \\\\  & =\\frac{8x+0}{2-0} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\,\\,4x \\\\  & =\\infty .\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070044/state.json" "file_sha256" "fcf78247d9a402fb67e5db2c4ea4f7384ca3af6e70cc708b70481b8ad348a81b"} {"question" "q-302235" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070044/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b0e21228d6346ad940cb7128271d38a4af8b3b4e91929c8c6677236e432cb17f"} {"question" "q-302235" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070044/state.json" "file_sha256" "fcf78247d9a402fb67e5db2c4ea4f7384ca3af6e70cc708b70481b8ad348a81b"} {"question" "q-302235" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\infty"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070044/state.json" "file_sha256" "fcf78247d9a402fb67e5db2c4ea4f7384ca3af6e70cc708b70481b8ad348a81b"} {"question" "q-339641" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the horizontal asymptote of $y=f(x)$ for $x>0$ with $f(x)=\\frac{|3-8x|}{4x+1}?$\n\nThe horizontal asymptote is $y=$\n\n{{field-1}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070044/state.json" "file_sha256" "fcf78247d9a402fb67e5db2c4ea4f7384ca3af6e70cc708b70481b8ad348a81b"} {"question" "q-339641" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For large positive values of $x,$ we have $|3-8x|=8x-3.$ Consequently, for $x\\to \\infty ,$ we get\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{|3-8x|}{4x+1}={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{8x-3}{4x+1}.\n$$\n\nThe horizontal asymptote for $x>0$ is $y={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }f(x).$ To find the horizontal asymptote, we apply the usual procedure of dividing the numerator and denominator by the highest power of $x$ in the denominator, which is $x.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{8x-3}{4x+1} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{8x}{x}-\\frac{3}{x})}{(\\frac{4x}{x}+\\frac{1}{x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(8-\\frac{3}{x})}{(4+\\frac{1}{x})} \\\\  & =\\frac{8-0}{4+0} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the horizontal asymptote is $y=2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070044/state.json" "file_sha256" "fcf78247d9a402fb67e5db2c4ea4f7384ca3af6e70cc708b70481b8ad348a81b"} {"question" "q-339641" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070044/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b0e21228d6346ad940cb7128271d38a4af8b3b4e91929c8c6677236e432cb17f"} {"question" "q-339641" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070044/state.json" "file_sha256" "fcf78247d9a402fb67e5db2c4ea4f7384ca3af6e70cc708b70481b8ad348a81b"} {"question" "q-339641" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070044/state.json" "file_sha256" "fcf78247d9a402fb67e5db2c4ea4f7384ca3af6e70cc708b70481b8ad348a81b"}] "usage" {"q-35831" 